-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1107: a named deadline carried past a breach. The buyer's
-- breach at 3 leaves the seller's duty standing, with 2 of its 5 still to
-- run; `sale named` should explore as `sale literal` does.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Buyer, Seller
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF pay, deliver

`five days` MEANS 5

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`sale literal` MEANS
        (PARTY Buyer MUST pay WITHIN 2 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Buyer)
  RAND  (PARTY Seller MUST deliver WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Seller)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`sale named` MEANS
        (PARTY Buyer MUST pay WITHIN 2 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Buyer)
  RAND  (PARTY Seller MUST deliver WITHIN `five days` HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Seller)
